WEBVTT

00:12:29.272 --> 00:12:31.483
But I have to tell you --
and sorry, Richard --

00:12:31.507 --> 00:12:34.841
but I never did like biology
field trips much --

00:12:34.865 --> 00:12:36.173
(Laughter)

00:12:36.197 --> 00:12:38.193
and I think we can just about make do

00:12:38.217 --> 00:12:40.317
with one every few hundred million years.

00:12:40.341 --> 00:12:42.358
(Laughter)

00:12:42.382 --> 00:12:49.338
So, in fact, intergalactic space
does contain all the prerequisites

00:12:49.362 --> 00:12:51.742
for the open-ended creation of knowledge.

00:12:52.357 --> 00:12:55.426
Any such cube anywhere in the universe

00:12:55.450 --> 00:13:00.035
could become the same kind
of hub that we are,